WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:04.700
The biggest movies of last year had some pretty
amazing moments, and we've devoured hours

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:07.600
of blockbuster excellence in order to experience
the best.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:12.160
Here are some of the most epic movie moments
from 2018 that are either pause-worthy in

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.280
order to take it all in, or deserve a rewind
to watch again.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.519
T'Challa's little sister Shuri is an engineering
genius.

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:22.560
So when she shows off all the technical gadgets
she's invented to help her big brother be

00:00:22.569 --> 00:00:26.289
the Black Panther, there are definitely a
bunch of moments when you might want to pause

00:00:26.289 --> 00:00:29.080
and examine each invention a little more closely.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.740
"Fully automated, like the old American movie
Baba used to watch."

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.340
But the most rewind-worthy moment comes toward
the end of the scene when T'Challa is checking

00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:40.030
out his new Black Panther suits.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:44.340
At first, Shuri implores him to give the suit
a kick, and it goes flying.

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:49.100
But as Shuri explains, the suit has absorbed
the kinetic energy left by T'Challa's kick,

00:00:49.109 --> 00:00:51.390
and the suit glows purple with its building
strength.

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:53.620
Then, Shuri asks him to attack again.

00:00:58.780 --> 00:00:59.860
"Delete that footage."

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:04.040
Shuri and the audience erupt in laughter at
the sight of the great Black Panther leveled

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:05.610
by a suit on a mannequin.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:07.660
It's a moment that's definitely worth a rewatch.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.260
Watching Avengers: Infinity War, it's hard
to say if anyone really believed that Thanos

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:16.180
was going to succeed in his plot to wipe out
half the population of the universe.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:20.850
But then he got all six Infinity Stones into
that gauntlet, and, well, everyone knows what

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:21.380
happened next.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.680
"Ohhhh snap."

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.820
After the snap, the dusting begins.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:30.800
First to go is Bucky, followed by Black Panther,
Groot, Scarlet Witch, and Falcon.

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:36.000
Out in space, Mantis, Drax, Star-Lord, and
Doctor Strange dissolve into space-dust.

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:40.259
But the most crushing dusting has got to be
that of Spider-Man, whose pleading with Tony

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.299
Stark is absolutely tragic.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.440
"I don't wanna go, I don't wanna go Mr Stark
Please.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:46.800
I don’t wanna go.

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.320
I don’t wanna go."

00:01:51.800 --> 00:01:55.060
How many people paused on Parker's heartbreaking
final moments?

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.109
We can only guess.

00:01:56.109 --> 00:02:00.070
Hopefully we'll find out soon enough if our
favorite Avengers are saved when Avengers:

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.420
Endgame hits theaters.

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:06.020
There are a few pretty awesome pause-worthy
moments in Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom,

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:10.600
2018's sequel to 2015's follow-up to the original
Jurassic Park franchise.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:16.440
This new movie introduced another scary dinosaur
hybrid, the Indoraptor, which, when it's finally

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.440
revealed, deserves a good pause just so we
can get a good look at it.

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.540
But Jurassic World: Fallen Kingdom's most
pause-worthy moment comes around the middle

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:33.360
of the film, when Claire, Owen, and their
gang try to evacuate the remaining dinos before

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.020
a volcano eruption kills them all.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:39.600
But the bigger dinosaurs move more slowly,
and one unlucky Brachiosaurus doesn't make

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.420
it off the island.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:45.040
In the saddest moment of the movie, the poor
guy is engulfed in smoke, and we hear a final,

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.440
heart-breaking bellow from the beast before
he collapses inside the cloud of ash.

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:53.140
“(sad dino)”

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.340
It deserves a pause just so we can get in
a moment of mourning before moving on to more

00:03:02.340 --> 00:03:02.840
action.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:07.440
For "technically" being a part of the X-Men
franchise, there are surprisingly few X-Men

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.900
characters in the first Deadpool movie, a
fact which Deadpool isn't shy about pointing

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:12.400
out.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.240
"It's a big house it’s funny that I only
see the two of you - it’s almost like the

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.980
studio couldn't afford another X-Man."

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:21.680
But Deadpool 2 takes it a bit further and
adds a fun cameo.

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.200
When Colossus brings a severely injured Wade
back to the X mansion, Wade remarks again

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:30.050
at the lack of X-Men characters willing to
make an appearance in his knock-off X-Men

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.380
movie...which is exactly when they appear.

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.860
"They can't just dust off one of the famous
X-Men?

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:36.770
How about that putz with the giant pigeon
wings?

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.870
What do those do anyway, carry him 3 feet
off the ground and snatch up the nearest muffin

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:41.360
crumb."

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.600
The fun gag is worth a pause just so we can
check out who's in the room: Xavier, Beast,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.320
Quicksilver, Cyclops, Storm, and Nightcrawler.

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:48.780
Mission: Impossible - Fallout - The HALO Jump

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:53.370
The latest installment in the Mission: Impossible
franchise features some of the most intense

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:55.640
action sequences in movie history.

00:03:55.770 --> 00:03:59.800
The biggest and most talked-about has got
to be the HALO jump star Tom Cruise takes

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.740
from a plane flying 25,000 feet in the air.

00:04:07.060 --> 00:04:11.100
The details behind what it took to capture
the jump on film are absolutely insane.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:15.420
Cruise is the first actor to perform such
a stunt, which is saying a lot about his willingness

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.860
to capture authenticity.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:21.880
He and the crew took over 100 jumps to get
the scene just right, while every jump required

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.800
at least 20 minutes of oxygen prep.

00:04:24.069 --> 00:04:28.180
And since the shot used in the movie happens
at sunset, they only had one chance per day

00:04:28.180 --> 00:04:29.780
to actually shoot the scene.

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:33.940
It's pause-worthy just because of how stunning
the whole thing is, and because once you watch

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.540
it, you simply have to know how it was done.

00:04:36.140 --> 00:04:39.760
Like the first movie, Marvel's Ant-Man and
the Wasp is filled with light-hearted and

00:04:39.760 --> 00:04:44.700
hilarious moments that counter the more dire
and serious aspects of the Marvel Universe.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:49.340
When Luis gets captured by Sonny Burch, he's
given a truth serum and forced to divulge

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:50.780
all he knows about Scott Lang.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:56.020
But this is Luis, Scott's blunt yet hilarious
best friend, so when he's given a truth serum,

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.460
you can bet he's going to tell you everything.

00:04:58.690 --> 00:05:02.780
Luis' story goes all the way back to when
he and Scott met in person, complete with

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:06.169
an enormous curly wig, then through his relationships
with Hope.

00:05:06.169 --> 00:05:07.540
"And Scotty is like you know what?

00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:10.680
My heart is like broken and I’ll probably
never find love again but DAMN if I wanna

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:11.180
kiss you."

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:15.039
The whole scene is definitely the funniest
sequence in the film, one that you'll probably

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:16.040
want to rewatch.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:20.940
Throughout the Star Wars prequel Solo: A Star
Wars story, Emilia Clarke's Qi'ra and Paul

00:05:20.949 --> 00:05:26.090
Bettany's Dryden Vos make references to a
higher criminal organization known as Crimson

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:26.580
Dawn.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:31.240
During the climax of the film, Qi'ra slays
Dryden, and abandons the love of her life,

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:32.060
Han Solo.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:36.479
It's at that point that she pledges allegiance
to Crimson Dawn via hologram, and a familiar

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.040
face pops up in the holographic communication
device: Darth Maul.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:44.740
It was a moment that left audience members
collectively gasping… but also asking, "How?"

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:48.900
Casual Star Wars movie viewers will recall
that Darth Maul met his end at the hands of

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.530
Obi-Wan Kenobi during The Phantom Menace.

00:05:51.530 --> 00:05:56.110
But fans of the animated series Clone Wars
and Rebels know that Maul survived his fall

00:05:56.110 --> 00:06:00.940
and became a crime boss who runs the organization
known as the Shadow Collective, which in turn

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:02.100
runs Crimson Dawn.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.160
Meanwhile, Solo takes place a couple of decades
after The Phantom Menace.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:10.780
Maul's reveal is definitely a pausable moment,
if only for fans to try and figure out if

00:06:10.789 --> 00:06:14.470
they're really seeing who they think they're
seeing, and work out the timeline of how the

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:17.280
former Sith lord turned crime boss ended up
there.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.160
Tom Hardy's Venom was one of the weirdest
movie experiences of last year, and very much

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:25.780
one of the most bizarre Marvel-inspired movies
that has ever existed.

00:06:25.780 --> 00:06:30.759
Fans can't seem to decide if it was amazing
or awful, intentionally campy or just bad

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:31.280
all around.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.819
But it does feature one of the most talked-about
moments of the cinematic year: the Eddie Brock

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:37.320
and Venom makeout session.

00:06:45.560 --> 00:06:47.120
Was it really between Eddie and Venom?

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:49.520
Was it between Eddie and his ex-girlfriend,
Anne?

00:06:49.729 --> 00:06:54.240
All we know is, when Venom is inhabiting Anne's
body, Venom leans in for a deep and intense

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.300
full-tongue kiss.

00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:59.680
Considering that Venom is in charge whenever
it's inhabiting someone, it certainly seems

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:01.800
like it was Venom who made the call to go
in deep.

00:07:02.200 --> 00:07:02.800
Pucker up.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:07.539
Through its use of sound, A Quiet Place became
one of the most innovative horror films in

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:08.040
years.

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:13.020
John Krasinski's directorial debut told the
story of a family struggling to survive after

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.540
a race of alien invaders took over the planet.

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.850
The creatures use sound to find their prey,
so being absolutely quiet is essential to

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:20.440
survival.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:24.640
The lack of sound in much of the film makes
the suspenseful moments even more intense

00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:26.120
and allows the tension to build.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:30.419
But the most pause-worthy moment comes right
at the end, when the mother Evelyn and her

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.800
deaf daughter Regen face off against the creatures
one final time.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:38.150
Regen realizes her cochlear implant
can be altered to emit a high-pitched sound

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.480
that wounds the creatures.

00:07:39.689 --> 00:07:43.960
Upon doing so, the one hunting them opens
up its face to reveal the inner workings of

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:44.960
the alien beast.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:51.260
“(Monster noise)”

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:55.400
Until that point, the creatures had stayed
mostly in the shadows, but this close look

00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:57.880
provides the best detail of the entire movie.

00:07:57.940 --> 00:08:02.039
It's a shot you'd definitely want to pause
just to get a good look… before Evelyn blows

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:02.860
its head off.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:06.280
If you love Queen, then you probably loved
Bohemian Rhapsody.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:10.680
Any of the musical moments in this film are
rewind-worthy, particularly the recording

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:12.700
session of "Bohemian Rhapsody" itself.

00:08:12.969 --> 00:08:17.039
But the most epic scene in the entire movie
is definitely the closing sequence, which

00:08:17.039 --> 00:08:21.439
revolves around the band's decision to perform
at Live Aid, a giant charity concert that

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.700
took place simultaneously in London and Philadelphia
in 1985.

00:08:25.909 --> 00:08:30.580
The movie pretty much recreates Queen's entire
performance, and Rami Malek has said he considers

00:08:30.580 --> 00:08:34.080
the concert the most important scene in the
film, telling CinemaBlend,

00:08:34.220 --> 00:08:37.760
"It is the culmination of what the trials
and tribulations were that got them there

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:41.160
in the first place, and they still have something
monumental to overcome.

00:08:41.160 --> 00:08:45.880
So I think if you look at this film, a lot
of it is about overcoming adversity and challenging

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.020
every aspect of yourself and your friends."

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:53.700
The 2018 Halloween is technically a direct
sequel to the 1978 original, even though there

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:55.700
have been six other movies between them.

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.440
This retconning of the series brings back
Jamie Lee Curtis as Laurie Strode and adds

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:03.380
a daughter named Karen and a granddaughter
named Allyson.

00:09:03.490 --> 00:09:07.820
The story follows the return of Michael Myers
as he escapes from a prison transport and

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:10.180
heads out on a killing spree on the hunt for
Laurie.

00:09:10.390 --> 00:09:15.780
Jamie Lee Curtis plays Laurie, now in her
60s, with a world-weariness and severe PTSD,

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:18.640
and she certainly has some moments of badassery
in the movie.

00:09:18.830 --> 00:09:23.000
But the moment many fans talked about most
has more to do with the usually sweet Judy

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:23.500
Greer.

00:09:23.620 --> 00:09:27.400
Though Laurie's daughter was taken from her
at an early age, Karen comes through for her

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:28.540
in a clutch moment.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:36.400
"I'm sorry I can't do it … Gotcha."

00:09:38.220 --> 00:09:42.570
The level of ridiculousness in The Meg reaches
pretty epic proportions, but despite being

00:09:42.570 --> 00:09:45.350
pretty goofy, the movie is still a whole lot
of fun.

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:50.181
Jason Statham stars as a guy trying to capture
and kill a really big shark a megalodon, to

00:09:50.181 --> 00:09:53.330
be precise and...that's about the entire premise.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:56.740
But what it lacks in story, it makes up for
by just by going all the way.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:00.950
The most epic scene in the entire movie comes
about midway through, when the gang of shark

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:04.870
hunters has captured the Meg and strung the
prehistoric creature up on their boat.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.000
Or at least, they think they've captured the
Meg.

00:10:07.120 --> 00:10:09.240
"Ahhhh, yeah, jellyfish"

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:20.380
The Meg took a crazy premise and made it even
crazier by making its massive villain even

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:20.880
bigger.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:24.940
There's nothing more exciting than a good
movie gunfight, but the one-sided showdown

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:28.000
from Hold the Dark isn't your typical Hollywood
shootout.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:32.560
This incredibly tense scene finds a group
of ill-equipped cops facing a very angry man

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:33.960
with a very big machine gun.

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:38.540
His name is Cheeon, and when the police roll
into his icy little village looking to arrest

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.810
him and his friend for murder he opens up
his second story window and unleashes hell

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:43.860
with an M60.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:47.930
The entire scene is nothing but ice, blood,
adrenaline, and fear.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:52.150
Bodies drop left and right, and the soundtrack
is filled with screaming men as Cheeon shoots

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.400
them over and over again.

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:57.310
It's like watching a clip from Saving Private
Ryan, and by the time the police put Cheeon

00:10:57.310 --> 00:11:01.440
down, we need to hit the pause button so we
can slow down our heart rate and try to get

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.200
our breath back.

